+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number). Each dish sold uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`; the
+  ledger `ref` is `sale:<ticket>`. Tickets imported before are skipped. If a
+  row is invalid or runs out of stock, nothing is imported and the error
+  (`bad_request`) names the row (`row 2` is the first data row). Answers
+  `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }` (dishes counts `qty`).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists per item
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`: theoretical use
+  from sales sold in those days (inclusive, UTC), actual use from every
+  `consume` movement in those days, and `difference = actual - theoretical`.
+  Items where both are zero are left out.
